        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add private AWS workspace service",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add a private, SSM-only AWS workspace path that uses the AWS SDK default credential chain and fails closed on account, Region, ECS task-role identity, and permissions\n- enforce allowlisted small instance classes, encrypted configurable gp3 storage, private-subnet placement, no public address or SSH, IMDSv2, bounded networking, exact tags, lifecycle evidence, and idempotent cleanup\n- add a dedicated internal ALB/ECS/PostgreSQL coordinator stack with separate execution, task, and workspace roles\n- document the client URL/token contract, readiness checks, create/status/delete lifecycle, live canary, retirement procedure, and source-blind behavior contract\n\n## Why\n\nThe portable AWS path assumes static credentials and large default workspace resources. A dedicated-account deployment needs renewable task-role credentials, strict placement checks, smaller cost-bounded workspaces, and an isolated controller that does not depend on a reusable shared control plane.\n\n## Security and operating boundary\n\n- the dedicated deployment rejects static AWS access keys and requires the expected account, Region, ECS metadata, and task-role identity before provisioning\n- workspaces use a private subnet, no public IPv4/IPv6 address, no key pair or inbound security-group rules, IMDSv2, SSM bootstrap, encrypted gp3 volumes, and exact ownership tags\n- the stack fixes this deployment to on-demand capacity and exposes instance type and volume limits only through an explicit allowlist\n- the Node image pins the AWS RDS CA bundle by checksum and scopes it to PostgreSQL through `sslrootcert`; it does not change process-wide TLS trust\n- this change contains no credentials, customer-specific source configuration, release changes, or version/tag changes\n\n## Verification\n\nValidated at exact head `95291c82933b39c46ef0f45aa47cb72f751fc05f` (tree `2f539adf1fb333c737e62be87a5424e07cfe7c54`):\n\n- `npm run format:check --prefix worker`\n- `npm run check --prefix worker`\n- `npm run check:node --prefix worker`\n- focused Worker suites: 576 passed across AWS private/deployment, fleet, HTTP, PostgreSQL storage, and coordinator runtime tests\n- `node --test scripts/aws-ecs-fargate-coordinator.test.js` (7 passed)\n- canonical structured branch autoreview: clean, confidence 0.83\n\nEarlier full-branch proof also passed Go build/vet/race, provider lifecycles, Worker lint/build/full test, docs, CloudFormation lint, and exact-head hosted CI; the final rebased head is additionally gated by the current hosted runs.\n\n## Live AWS acceptance\n\nAuthenticated acceptance passed in account `433939225574`, Region `us-west-2`, at exact head `95291c82933b39c46ef0f45aa47cb72f751fc05f`:\n\n- dedicated foundation and coordinator stacks are `UPDATE_COMPLETE`; the coordinator runs privately on ECS Fargate with separate execution, task, and workspace roles\n- exact-head image tag `95291c82933b` is pinned and running as digest `sha256:ee582b7d37873a0fb17eb40d5b8e68dbcb3229770c88f71c781c6b0d248f54b9`; ECS container and internal ALB target are healthy\n- readiness returned `{\"ok\":true}` through a certificate-verified SSM tunnel; no public control-plane route was used\n- canary workspace `exact-head-95291c82-1783766338` / lease `cbx_376391180788` reached `ready` on instance `i-0d94f79089b0f8e1c`\n- posture: `t3a.small`, private IP only, no key pair, private subnet `subnet-0a9ed271ea27811da`, workspace security group `sg-0232b5f3976fa40ca`, IMDSv2 required with hop limit 1 and metadata tags/IPv6 disabled\n- storage: encrypted 20 GiB gp3 volume `vol-0dff02e94b3fe0bc3`, delete-on-termination enabled\n- SSM bootstrap command `09bdd298-9cf2-42c0-b683-587566dce9a3` completed `Success` with response code 0 and retained CloudWatch output\n- identical create returned the same provider resource; delete reached `stopped`; repeated delete remained `stopped`\n- EC2 instance terminated and the encrypted workspace volume was absent after cleanup\n- the temporary private SSM proof client and its volume were also terminated/deleted; no proof resources remain\n\nNo credential or bearer value is included in this PR or its proof.\n",
